    "result_text": "The full suite is green (44 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**`Localities.java`** \u2014 added a `REGION_POSTCODES` range table (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) and a new two-arg `region(String city, String postcode)` overload. It looks up the region by postcode range first, and only falls back to the existing city-to-region table when the postcode is absent, non-numeric, or in no known range. The original one-arg `region(String city)` is retained because `ValidateOwnerFields` legitimately needs the city's expected region to validate a submitted postcode (using the postcode-preferred method there would be circular).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now calls `Localities.region(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())`.\n\n**Behavior:** known cities without a postcode still map to the same region (Cp17). A postcode in a known range wins over the city \u2014 e.g. an unknown city with postcode `3000` yields `VIC` (Cp30), which disambiguates same-named cities.\n\nAll 44 tests pass, including the new `Cp30Tests`.",
