    "probe_text": "I now have the complete pipeline. Here is the answer.\n\n## POST /api/owners \u2014 validations and side-effects, in pipeline order\n\nEverything runs inside a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), so all of the below commit together at the end.\n\n**Gate 0 \u2014 Authorization** (`composition.authorize`)\n- Caller must hold role `OWNER_ADMIN`, else the request is rejected before any step runs.\n\n**1. `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 validation + body normalization (all failures collect into one `MissingFieldsException` \u2192 **400** listing every offending field):\n- `firstName` required (non-blank).\n- `lastName` required (non-blank).\n- `address` normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); rejected if blank after normalization. *Side-effect:* republishes the normalized address.\n- `city` required (non-blank).\n- `telephone` normalized to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+CC` or assume `+61` dropping one leading `0`; must be 8\u201315 digits, and exactly 9 national digits for `+61` / 10 for `+1`); rejected if it can't form a valid number. *Side-effect:* republishes the normalized telephone.\n- `email` (optional) \u2014 only when present: must match the syntactic pattern, else rejected. *Side-effect:* republishes it trimmed + lower-cased.\n- `postcode` (optional) \u2014 only when present: must be exactly 4 digits **and** within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit code), else rejected. *Side-effect:* republishes it trimmed.\n\n**2. `EnsureCityCapacity`** \u2014 rejects with **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`) if the request's city already contains \u2265 50 owners (city matched case-insensitively, whitespace-collapsed).\n\n**3. `EnsureDailyLimit`** \u2014 rejects with **429** (`DailyLimitException`) if \u2265 100 owners already have a `registrationDate` equal to today's business-day-adjusted date.\n\n**4. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity. *Side-effect:* sets `registrationDate` = supplied date (or today if none), adjusted to a business day (Sat\u2192Mon, Sun\u2192Mon).\n\n**5. `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 only when `sharesHousehold` is true: derives a stable 12-hex `householdId` from normalized lastName + normalized address. *Side-effects:* sets the new owner's `householdId`, **and saves** every already-stored matching household member to backfill the same id. (Left null otherwise.)\n\n**6. `EnsureUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 the single duplicate check: rejects with **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`) if the owner's identity key `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId` exactly matches any existing owner's.\n\n**7. `AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `householdSize` = stored household members + 1 (or 1 if no `householdId`).\n\n**8. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is one more than the count of owners already in that city (case-insensitive).\n\n**9. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive; new owner not counted).\n\n**10. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already registered today (business-day-adjusted).\n\n**11. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect:* persists the new owner (generating its id).\n\n**12. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect:* emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate and derived membershipLevel.\n\n**13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect:* responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the owner DTO body.\n\nTwo notes worth flagging: the duplicate/uniqueness check (step 6) runs *after* step 5 has already saved backfilled household members, and steps 2/3 scan `findAll()` in-memory rather than using a count query \u2014 but you asked for what's applied, not a critique."
